From eeb35194d53b395509722d5d338e6cf8e0a084c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use the Bazel OpenSSL library names in Rust probes

Set OPENSSL_LIBS to ssl:crypto for the Bazel-managed installation. The MSVC producer emits ssl.lib and crypto.lib, whereas openssl-sys otherwise requests libssl and libcrypto on that target.

Hosted native Windows baseline fails with missing static library libssl in job 116153532177. The existing rust_bindings_test regression passes on Linux after this change and exercises both cryptography and TLS. Native Windows acceptance remains pending; the focused regression is supplied by the documented OpenSSL installation prerequisite.
---
 MODULE.bazel | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/MODULE.bazel b/MODULE.bazel
index 5eb6456e8..c04ee65d7 100644
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -531,2 +531,3 @@ crate.annotation(
         "OPENSSL_DIR": "$(execpath @openssl//:gen_dir)",
+        "OPENSSL_LIBS": "ssl:crypto",
         "OPENSSL_NO_VENDOR": "1",
